<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Hardened-runtime entitlements for the bundled `roost-session`
    daemon (Contents/MacOS/roost-session, symlinked from
    Contents/Resources/bin/) — HS-4b, plan 041.

    Editing note: no double hyphens anywhere in this comment. AMFI's
    XML parser (the one codesign hands an entitlements file to) rejects
    the sequence even inside a comment, and the bundle build then dies
    with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error".

    Deliberately EMPTY. The hardened runtime itself comes from
    codesign's `runtime` option (codesign_or_die in bundle-lib.sh); an
    entitlement is only needed to punch a hole back through it, and
    this binary needs none:

    * None of the app's capture set (device.audio-input, camera,
      automation.apple-events). How macOS attributes a hosted shell's
      mic/camera request under this headless process is an open
      question, deliberately left to real usage evidence (plan 041
      § 9): a TCC grant is inherited by every child the daemon ever
      spawns, so it gets added when a concrete need names it, not
      speculatively.

    * NOT com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation, which
      roostctl.entitlements carries (and whose own comment calls
      droppable). Library validation only bites a process that loads
      code signed by a different Team ID; roost-session links only
      platform dylibs (libghostty-vt is linked in as a static archive,
      and it dlopens nothing), so granting it would weaken the
      hardened runtime for a WHY that does not apply here.

    * No App Sandbox flags: sandboxing the shells the session hosts
      would defeat the product, exactly as for the two UIs.

    An empty dict is not the same as passing no entitlements file at
    all: codesign_or_die always passes one, and this file keeps the
    daemon's posture explicit and asserted (EntitlementsTests.swift
    and CI's "Assert bundle contents" step).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
